The <ansi fg="command">spell</ansi> command is used to create and list spells (admin only).

<ansi fg="command">spell list</ansi>
List all spells in the game.

<ansi fg="command">spell list [search term]</ansi>
List spells matching the search term. Wildcards supported, e.g.:
  <ansi fg="command">spell list *fire*</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">spell create</ansi>
Launch an interactive prompt to create a new spell. You will be asked for:
  - Spell name
  - Unique spell ID (used as the cast alias)
  - Short description
  - Spell type (harm-single, help-single, area, etc.)
  - Conviction cost
  - Wait rounds
  - Casting difficulty

<ansi fg="command">spell create [existing spell name or ID]</ansi>
Start the creation prompt pre-filled with an existing spell's values (for duplication).

Note: After creation, you must write the spell's effect logic in its
generated script file before it will do anything in-game.

Required permissions: <ansi fg="yellow">spell.create</ansi>, <ansi fg="yellow">spell.list</ansi>
